+/*
+ * Galaxy A8 (2018, jackpotlte) Wi-Fi / Bluetooth, stage 2: wake Samsung's WLBT ("Maxwell") core and see whether its
+ * firmware runs. Boot-arg a8wlbt=1; nothing happens without it.
+ *
+ * Facts (stock BOOT.img device tree; Samsung's SM-A530F kernel, GPL-2.0, read for facts only:
+ * drivers/misc/samsung/scsc/platform_mif.c, mif_reg_S5E7885.h, mxman.c, fwhdr.c, mx140_file.c):
+ *   shared memory 0xE9000000, 4 MB (reserved-memory wifibt_if): the firmware runs from it, R4-relative address 0
+ *   mailbox 0x120C0000 (MAILBOX_WLBT): ISSR(n) = 0x80 + 4n are the mailboxes; INTMR0/1, INTCR0/1 masks and clears
+ *   PMU 0x11C80000: WIFI_CTRL_NS 0x140 (PWRON bit 1, RESET_SET bit 2), WIFI_CTRL_S 0x144 (START bit 3),
+ *        WIFI_STAT 0x148, WIFI2AP_MEM_CONFIG0 0x7300 (size >> 12) / CONFIG1 0x7304 (base >> 12),
+ *        WLBT_BOOT_TEST_RST_CFG 0x7330 (0: boot from DRAM), EXT_REGULATOR_SHARED_OPTION 0x3648 bit 2
+ *   SMC 0x82000710 (WLBT_TZASC = 0, base, size): lets the core reach the shared memory through TrustZone
+ *   start: firmware image copied to offset 0; mailbox 0 = entry point (header +40), 1 = the configuration's
+ *        address (0 here: there is none yet), 2 = 0xbcdeedcb, 3 = start flags (0); then PWRON, RESET_SET off, START.
+ *   firmware: /sweet/fw/mx140.bin (from the phone's /vendor/etc/wifi; not in git). Header "smxf" at +8, runtime
+ *        length +36, entry +40, build id +48, R4 panic record offset +176.
+ *
+ * Stage 2 result (ios60n): the core ran and wrote its panic record (version 2, 0xd4 bytes) with mailbox 1 = 0.
+ *
+ * Stage 3 (this file): mailbox 1 now points at a configuration block in the heap right after the firmware's runtime
+ * length, laid out as Samsung's mxconf (facts from mxconf.h, mifstream.c, cpacket_buffer.c, mifintrbit.c, mxman.c,
+ * mxmgmt_transport.c, gdb_transport.c, mxlog_transport.c; packed little-endian):
+ *   u32 magic 0x79828486; u16 major 0, minor 1; then four stream pairs/streams. A stream = buffer offset, packet
+ *   count, packet size, read-index offset, write-index offset (u32 each, offsets relative to the shared memory),
+ *   u8 read interrupt bit, u8 write interrupt bit. Pairs are (to AP, from AP).
+ *   management (8-byte packets, 64), gdb R4 and gdb M4 (4-byte packets, 512 each), mxlog (to AP only, 4-byte, 4096).
+ *   Interrupt bits in the order Linux allocates them (to-host bits count up from 0; from-host R4/M4 from 1, bit 0
+ *   reserved for the gdb out streams): mgmt in r1 w0, mgmt out r1 w2, gdb R4 in r3 w2, out r3 w0, gdb M4 in r1 w4,
+ *   out r5 w0, mxlog in r4 w6. To-AP buffers start filled with 0xff.
+ * The probe polls (no interrupt handler): it reports the to-AP write indices and, at the end, the management packets
+ * (MM_START_IND = channel 0 payload 0 is what Linux waits for), the first mxlog words and the whole panic record.
+ * Logged as "SWEET A8 WLBT:". The core is left as it ends; a reboot resets it.
+ */
